## SETTLED PREMISES — re-inlined, with their warrants, so you need not re-derive them

* **Book I v2.01 GOVERNS over the 2005 PEM, and the PEM says so itself**:
  `ppc_pem_32and64_2005.txt:302` — *"This book does not attempt to replace the PowerPC Architecture
  specification (version 2.01) … which remains the defining manual."*
* **`MASK(x, y)` WRAPS when x > y** — Book I `:578`: *"1s in positions x through y (wrapping if
  x > y) and 0s elsewhere."*
* **Book I's high-order-clearing sentence is SCOPED and the PEM's is UNCONDITIONAL.** Book I
  `:4195-4196` says *"For all the uses given above, the high-order 32 bits of register RA are
  cleared"* — qualified to the programming-note uses enumerated immediately above, **every one of
  which fixes a NON-WRAPPING (MB, ME)**. The PEM carries that same qualified sentence at `:30074`
  **and an unconditional one at `:30065`**. The unconditional claim is **absent from Book I**, and
  neither qualified sentence reaches the wrapping case — so Book I's normative RTL governs it.
* `rlwinm`'s RTL is at Book I `:4125-4137`: `r <- ROTL32((RS)32:63, n); m <- MASK(MB+32, ME+32);
  RA <- r & m`.

