Book I explicitly says that 32-bit execution mode still writes all 64 register bits. Discarding the high half is therefore justified only for a genuinely 32-bit implementation. The permitted source file does not define `MODE_uint_t`, `reg`, or `update_cr0`, so it cannot settle how that distinction is implemented.

I’m finishing the boundary enumeration and identifying mutations that the probe cannot observe.
